{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Quotient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Quotient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Submodule.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Quotient.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Defs"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.not_normalFormBasis_of_not_gs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.not_normalFormBasis_of_not_gs","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L293-L306","doc":"**What a failed GS basis costs**, once the CD-lemma is available: the normal\nforms of a non-confluent system are *not* a basis of the algebra it presents.\n\nThis is why the Bokut–Shiao completion is not optional for the Hecke route to\n`H_k`, `k > 4`. `UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.hecke_not_gs_basis_four` refutes\nclause (i) for the uncompleted system at `n = 4`; by Theorem 4.4 clause (iii)\nfails too, so its 24 reduced words cannot be assumed to be a basis of\n`kC(X)/Id(S)` — they have to be obtained some other way, which is exactly what\n`QOU.Machinery.HeckeH4AlgebraLaws` does by hand, and exactly what does not scale\npast `n = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.CompositionDiamond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.CompositionDiamond","kind":"def","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L284-L291","doc":"**Composition–Diamond lemma**, one-object case: being a Gröbner–Shirshov\nbasis is equivalent to the normal-form monomials being a basis of the quotient.\n\nBokut–Chen–Li 2011, Theorem 4.4 (i) ⟺ (iii), via the Remark on one-object\ncategories. Stated, not proved — see the section note. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalFormBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalFormBasis","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L241-L253","doc":"**The conclusion of the composition lemma**, as a proposition about the\nquotient: the classes of the normal-form monomials form a `k`-basis of\n`A = k⟨G⟩ / (Σ)`.\n\n`composition_lemma` states only `reduce (reduce f) = reduce f` and asserts *this*\nin its docstring. Anything wanting the PBW/monomial-basis conclusion — the Hecke\nroute to `H_k` for `k > 4`, the flatness argument, the \"monomial basis of `A`\"\nhalf of the main theorem — needs this, and can now name it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalFormMonomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalFormMonomial","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L235-L239","doc":"The monomials in normal form for `sys`: those no rule's leading monomial\ndivides (as an infix). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.relation_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.relation_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L221-L226","doc":"Every relation dies in the quotient — the defining property, and a check that\n`systemIdeal` is the right submodule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.toQuot_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.toQuot_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L217-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.toQuot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.toQuot","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L213-L215","doc":"The projection `k⟨G⟩ ↠ A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QuotAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.QuotAlg","kind":"def","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L209-L211","doc":"**The quotient `A = k⟨G⟩ / (Σ)`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.mem_systemIdeal_of_context","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.mem_systemIdeal_of_context","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L199-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.systemIdeal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.systemIdeal","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L194-L197","doc":"**The ideal `I = (Σ)`**, as a submodule of `k⟨G⟩` spanned by the relations in\nall monomial contexts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.relationContexts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.relationContexts","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L189-L192","doc":"The generating set: every relation of `sys`, in every monomial context. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instModule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instModule","kind":"instance","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L165-L174","doc":"**…and a `k`-module.** Note `zero_smul`: this is the law that fails on the\nnose for `AlgElement`, because `smul 0 f` keeps `f.support`. Here it holds,\nbecause here elements *are* their coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instAddCommGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instAddCommGroup","kind":"instance","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L154-L163","doc":"**`k⟨G⟩` is an additive group.** Every law is its coefficient-wise counterpart\nin `k`, which is what `ext` reduces it to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_smul","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L149-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_neg","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L143-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_add","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L136-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L134-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instSMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instSMul","kind":"instance","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L128-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instNeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instNeg","kind":"instance","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L123-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instAdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instAdd","kind":"instance","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L118-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.instZero","kind":"instance","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L112-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.ext","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L105-L110","doc":"**Elements are determined by their coefficients** — the property `AlgElement`\nlacked, and the reason this quotient exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff_mk","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L102-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.coeff","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L98-L100","doc":"Coefficient extraction descends: it is exactly what `CoeffEq` preserves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.mk_eq_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.mk_eq_mk","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L94-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg.mk","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L91-L92","doc":"The class of a representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.FreeAlg","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L85-L87","doc":"The free associative algebra `k⟨G⟩`, as a quotient of the representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.algSetoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.algSetoid","kind":"instance","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L76-L79","doc":"The setoid that turns the representation into the thing it represents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.coeffEq_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.coeffEq_trans","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L72-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.coeffEq_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.coeffEq_symm","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L69-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.coeffEq_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.coeffEq_refl","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Quotient.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0}]}